-- title:
--   Roof reduction commutes place by place with both degeneracy maps
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ and let $q$ be a prime not dividing $N$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, write $\kappa$ for its residue field, and let $\ell\ne q$ be a prime. Assume the four inclusions are integral: the degeneracy inclusion `heckeAlphaBar` and the $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$ map `heckeBetaBar` from the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the level-$N$ modular function field into the level-$N\ell$ one, and their characteristic-$q$ counterparts `heckeAlphaC` (the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,N$ into `charLDegeneracyRoof` $\kappa\,N\,\ell$, the $\kappa$-field generated by $\tilde j$, $\tilde j_N$, $\tilde j_\ell$, $\tilde j_{N\ell}$) and `heckeBetaC` (induced by the substitution $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$). Assume every nonzero element of the two levels over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and of the roof over $\kappa$ has a degree-zero principal divisor, and that every place of the roof has residue degree $1$ over $\kappa$. Let $R_1$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ to the level-$N$ field with residue field `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,N$ (a valuation subring of it whose elements restrict over $A$, together with a surjection onto the residue field with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$, each nonzero element becoming integral with nonzero residue after scaling by $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), and let $r_1$ be a map from places of the level-$N$ field to places of `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,N$ such that for every $f$ in $R_1$ with nonzero residue and every divisor $D$ with $D(P)=\operatorname{ord}_P f$ for all $P$, the pushforward of $D$ along $r_1$ satisfies $(\,r_{1*}D)(Q)=\operatorname{ord}_Q(\bar f)$ for all $Q$. Assume furthermore that $j$ and its $N$-fold $q$-expansion lie in $R_1$ with residues $\tilde j$ and $\tilde j_N$. Then there exist a regular prolongation $R_\ell$ of $A$ to the level-$N\ell$ field with residue field `charLDegeneracyRoof` $\kappa\,N\,\ell$ and a map $r_\ell$ on places such that: $r_\ell$ has the same divisor compatibility with $R_\ell$ as $r_1$ has with $R_1$; for every $f$ in $R_1$, $\alpha f$ and $\beta f$ lie in $R_\ell$ with residues $\alpha_{\mathrm c}(\bar f)$ and $\beta_{\mathrm c}(\bar f)$; for every place $v$ of the level-$N$ field the degree of the pullback of $(v,1)$ along `heckeAlphaBar` equals the degree of the pullback of $(r_1 v,1)$ along `heckeAlphaC`, and likewise for $\beta$; and for every place $W$ of the level-$N\ell$ field, $(r_\ell W)$ restricted along `heckeAlphaC` equals $r_1$ of $W$ restricted along `heckeAlphaBar`, and the same with $\beta$ in place of $\alpha$.
--
--   This is the place-by-place form of the existence of a reduction of the level-$N\ell$ modular function field at a place above $q$ with $q\nmid N\ell$: beyond the divisor-, residue- and degree-level compatibilities, it asserts that the two squares relating reduction to the degeneracy maps $\alpha$ and $\beta$ commute on individual places, so that one knows onto which point of the level-$N$ fibre a given roof place restricts. It is used in the construction of place specialisations compatible with both degeneracy maps for a model of the modular curve in characteristic $q$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_charLDegeneracyRoof_regularProlongation_heckeCompat_restrictAlong_eq_of_ne.lean

